WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.320
[MUSIC]

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:09.940
You can control a sprite's properties in your program by using dot

00:00:09.984 --> 00:00:16.864
notation. First, connect the label of the sprite to the label of the property with a dot.

00:00:17.744 --> 00:00:19.824
Now you can use this just like a variable.

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:29.928
So, for example, mySprite.x gets 200. We'll update the sprite's x location to 200.

00:00:29.953 --> 00:00:35.753
mySprite.width gets 50. We'll update the sprite's width to 50. The next time you

00:00:35.753 --> 00:00:39.937
call drawSprites, these new property values will be used to draw the sprite.

00:00:39.937 --> 00:00:43.937
Sprites can have tons of properties.

00:00:43.937 --> 00:00:49.922
As you get familiar with them, they'll give you powerful controls over what your sprites look like and can do.

00:00:49.922 --> 00:00:53.262
[MUSIC]
